        <body>
            <div xml:id="d735">

                <pb facs="0799" n="790" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg790"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">617.003/251: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-07T19:00:00-05:00">February 7, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. Your 16, February 7, 1 p.m. Proclamation with dates left blank signed by
                    President this morning. You are therefore authorized to proceed at once to the
                    exchange of notes. The Department assumes that text of notes will be that
                    supplied by Department in its No. 8 of February 1, 5 p.m. as corrected in No. 9
                    of January [<hi rendition="#italic">February</hi>] 3, 5 p.m.<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d735-f1"/> and amplified in No. 10 of February 5, 3 p.m. <pb
                        facs="0800" n="791" xml:id="pg791"/> If the notes are exchanged on February
                    8, the date to be inserted in the second paragraph is March 10. Press
                    announcement containing text of notes to be exchanged between you and the
                    Foreign Minister, will be issued upon receipt of information from you that notes
                    have been exchanged.</p>
                <p>Department will inform you of date upon which announcement will appear in
                    newspapers here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
